{
  "schema_version": 1,
  "_comment": [
    "The role table (D46). Every guard and the apply scripts read this file; none of them names a profile, model or display name.",
    "profiles: one row per Hermes profile (\"default\" is Hermes's own name for the root profile). dir: the profile's folder under",
    "~/.hermes (default \"profiles/<name>\"); soul: its rules file in docs/hermes-local/soul/; worker: the worker kind it runs (one of",
    "its role's workers); display_name: what the owner calls it, used only to spot cards that target its own configuration.",
    "roles: the permissions the guards enforce (assignable, may_answer_for_owner, workspace, may_*, allowed_overrides), background_review and config",
    "(hermes config keys set at apply), and what apply installs: platform_toolsets, skills_disabled and hooks (pre_tool_call,",
    "fail-closed; file = a repo hook copied to <profile dir>/hooks/<file name>, command = a /workspace/bin hook run in place;",
    "workers = only for profiles whose worker is listed). A profile with no row gets fallback_role, which opens nothing.",
    "may_answer_for_owner (every role, true on one): the coordinator the reply poller runs as: free to comment on any card, and its comments count as the owner's answers. Never derived from assignable.",
    "requirements (every role): what a model needs to hold the role: tool_calling, vision (true = needed), min_context_tokens, allowed_data_classes (class names from .stella/data-policy.json). Read with: bin/roles.py requirements <role>.",
    "Owner-write path (F1 W4): owner_settings = files no role reads or writes or commits (they hold values); owner_data = paths no role writes or lets a worker commit, but every role may read (tracked data: .stella); owner_commands = commands no role runs (the apply tool, the settings tool, the merge); data_index = the data index, which names the apply tool's backup folder (owner values in clear: no role reads or writes it); worker_markers = the environment variables that mark a worker's process; worker_pins = the variables the box sets to the worker's workspace and branch. Every guard reads these lists here; a table missing one is invalid and every guard refuses everything.",
    "Three layers (F1 W4 round 2; a text guard cannot decide what a shell will do): (1) a role that runs in the OS box (sandbox.boxed_profiles) has the box as its boundary; (2) a role that does not (runs_unboxed true: the coordinator and the fallback role) has hooks that refuse every write: a hook entry with writes \"refused\" on each tool of write_tools, none with writes \"judged\" (the write guard); (3) whatever reaches a card branch meets the merge check (bin/merge-card.sh), which refuses owner data and flags boundary_paths and the hook files. owner_data = the table's own list; the owner data the index names (the index, every row with owner_only true) is added by bin/roles.py owner_paths. owner_commands_by_name = owner commands refused wherever their name appears in a command text.",
    "Add a profile: one row under profiles, then bin/apply-hermes-local.sh. Add a role: one entry under roles, then the same."
  ],
  "fallback_role": "unlisted",
  "protected": {
    "_comment": "The one protected-path list (D40, D46): the builders' write guard and the card guard both read it.",
